<title>NEW ZEALAND: Bank of New Zealand drops NZ mortgage rates.</title>
<headline>Bank of New Zealand drops NZ mortgage rates.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of New Zealand said late on Tuesday it had joined other banks in cutting its mortgage lending rates.</p>
<p>The BNZ's floating mortgage lending rate dropped to 8.95 percent from 9.4 percent, effective from August 4.</p>
<p>The bank's one-year fixed lending rate fell to 8.1 percent from 8.25 percent, while the two and three year fixed rates fell to 8.6 percent from 8.75 percent. The fixed rates are effective from July 7.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
